    "source": "임의 합성 (실제 강의자료 대용 PoC 픽스처)",
    "body": "# Common Cardiovascular Pathologies\n\nThis week we cover several disorders of the heart and vascular system.\n\n## Rhythm and rate\n\nThe most common arrhythmia in our ED is **tachycardia**, often presenting alongside chest pain. **Bradycardia** may indicate sinus node dysfunction.\n\n## Inflammation\n\n**Endocarditis** (inflammation of the heart's inner lining) requires urgent antibiotic therapy. **Pericarditis** is similar but affects the surrounding sac.\n\n## Ischemic and structural disease\n\n**Myocardial infarction** is death of heart muscle tissue from coronary occlusion. **Atherosclerosis** — the buildup of fatty plaque in arteries — is the major risk factor. Long-standing **hypertension** often produces **cardiomegaly**. Right-sided heart failure can present with **hepatomegaly** and peripheral edema.\n\n## Diagnostics and management\n\n**Angiography** is the gold standard for visualizing coronary arteries. Patients with multiple risk factors are typically referred to a **cardiologist** for ongoing management. Common labs include screening for **hyperlipidemia** and **hyperglycemia**."
  },
